// A league's two halves. Fantasy conferences, not the NBA's: a team is put
// in one when it is created and the commissioner can move it.
// League Intel — what a team says it is doing this season.
//
// Self-reported: it is set by that team's own owner and read-only to everybody
// else, which is the whole point. Nothing in the rule book enforces it and
// nothing in the cap engine reads it; it exists so the other eleven owners
// know who is worth calling about a trade.
enum TeamIntelStatus {
  contending
  rebuilding
  buying
  selling
}

